.TH tumd n 0.1 tclutils
.SH tclutils::tumd
.PP
Small dependency\-free Markdown helpers for Tcl.
.PP
\fBtumd\fR is intentionally not a full Markdown system. It provides a practical CommonMark subset for scripts and CI: Markdown\-to\-HTML fragments, ATX heading extraction, table\-of\-contents generation, and YAML front matter splitting.
.SS Package
.CS
package require tclutils::tumd 0.1
.CE
.SS API
.CS
::tclutils::tumd::toHtml markdown
::tclutils::tumd::headings markdown
::tclutils::tumd::toc markdown
::tclutils::tumd::frontmatter markdown
.CE
.SS Example
.CS
package require tclutils::tumd

set md {# Title

A **short** paragraph.}
puts [::tclutils::tumd::toHtml $md]
puts [::tclutils::tumd::toc $md]
.CE
.SS "Supported subset"
.PP
Blocks:
.IP \(bu
ATX headings (\fB#\fR to \fB######\fR)
.IP \(bu
paragraphs
.IP \(bu
fenced code blocks using backticks or tildes
.IP \(bu
blockquotes
.IP \(bu
flat ordered and unordered lists
.IP \(bu
horizontal rules
.PP
Inline constructs:
.IP \(bu
code spans
.IP \(bu
bold and italic
.IP \(bu
links and images
.IP \(bu
autolinks
.IP \(bu
hard line breaks with two trailing spaces
.SS Limits
.PP
\fBtumd\fR does not implement nested lists, Setext headings, GFM tables, reference\-style links, raw HTML passthrough, or a full Markdown AST. For larger Markdown workflows, use the mdstack/docir toolchain.
